bfloat16 sin, cos, tanh, exp, log, exp2, log2, sqrt and rsqrt of finite nonzero inputs: within the stated ulps of f64 with subnormals kept (skipped on Metal and on CUDA's f32 intrinsics, accepted vendor behaviour claimed by their own contracts): true
Metal bfloat16 sin, cos, tanh, exp, log, exp2, log2, sqrt and rsqrt: NaN where f64 gives NaN, the signed zero or infinity where f64 rounds to one, otherwise within the stated ulps of f64 -- for exp, log, exp2, log2, sqrt and rsqrt, of f64 at the input or the f32 result flushed from subnormal to zero: true
bfloat16 pow and fmod over +-0, +-inf, NaN and dyadic operands: NaN where C gives NaN, otherwise the signed zero or infinity C gives, or within the stated ulps of it -- CUDA's f32 pow within __powf's 2 + 2 |y log2 |x|| -- and fmod exactly (every backend): true
